1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Why does Portswiger exist?

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Well, when I got Portswiger going, I'd had a couple of jobs before, and I'd also worked as a consultant,

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,000
and I'd seen many businesses from the inside, how they worked, how people behaved.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
And the way I thought about sitting at Portswiger was in many ways a reaction against things that I'd seen happening elsewhere.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Fundamentally, I wanted work to be fun. I thought if we can make sure that the core stuff we're working on is fun,

6
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:43,000
and also take away the things that stop work being fun, then we're onto a good thing.

7
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:51,000
For me, fun means working on hard problems, building cool things to solve them, and sharing those with other people.

8
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:56,000
It also means being surrounded by great people who work well together.

9
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,000
And fun might mean different things for different people.

10
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Having fun doesn't mean slacking. We work hard, we're ambitious, we want to achieve the best we possibly can.

11
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
If we do something at all, we aim to do it to an exceptional standard.

12
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
We certainly want to be commercially successful, and we ought to be, given our strengths,

13
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:26,000
but only if that's consistent with our other goals, not at any cost.

14
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Certainly not at the cost of stopping having fun, or of treating our people badly.

15
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:38,000
We see looking after our people as an end in itself.

16
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:45,000
We pay people well, we give everyone share options so they can have a long-term stake in the value that we're building together.

17
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,000
But obviously, living well isn't just about having money.

18
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:00,000
It's about being fulfilled, learning new things, being healthy and free of stress, having good relationships with the people you interact with.

19
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Many things.

20
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Our culture, the ways we work, our working environment, are all really about looking after our people's wellbeing in the full sense.

21
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:18,000
I think one sure thing that kills your wellbeing is to get greedy and selfish.

22
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Thinking that you'd be really happy if only you had a bit more money is a fast-track way to never being happy at all.

23
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:31,000
And when companies act in that way, it's bad for everyone.

24
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:36,000
It's far more rewarding to strive to be a force for good in the world.

25
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:41,000
I think at Port Swinger, we can be incredibly proud of what we've done.

26
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:47,000
We've obviously created some fantastic products and innovations for our industry.

27
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:53,000
We've created learning and knowledge that have benefited a whole generation of people.

28
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Our products are cheap.

29
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
We give away our knowledge for free.

30
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
We give a lot of money to charity.

31
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:04,000
If we can have fun while making the world a better place, that's a pretty good place to be.

32
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,000
In a nutshell, that's why Port Swinger exists.

33
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
To have fun, look after each other and do the right things.

